// Auto-generated by matugen — Material You
//
// ── The WHOLE config.kdl, not a colour fragment (D-01, quick task 260820-0ha) ──
// Measured this session, three ways, non-empty byte capture asserted on
// every branch: a theme defined INLINE in config.kdl live-reloads a running
// session (14001 bytes captured, old fg SGR gone, new one present, no
// restart). A theme in a separate themes/<name>.kdl applies at start but
// does NOT live-reload (4901 bytes, a real negative). Touching config.kdl
// does not make zellij re-read a separate themes dir either (7694 bytes,
// still absent). KDL has no include/source mechanism, so the
// "app sources a matugen fragment" pattern fish/fzf use here is
// UNAVAILABLE for zellij — the only way to make colours live-reload is to
// render the entire config, inline theme included, from this one template.
//
// ── output_path is the STATE DIR, not ~/.config/zellij/config.kdl directly ──
// A task brief for this work said to target ~/.config/zellij/config.kdl.
// That shape cannot work, measured in code, three independent reasons:
//   1. commit.sh promotes exactly one directory:
//      `rsync -a --delete "$rendered_dir"/ "$STATE_DIR"/` where
//      rendered_dir="$tmp$STATE_DIR". matugen's -p prefixes the tmp dir
//      onto the resolved absolute output_path, so a template targeting
//      ~/.config/zellij/config.kdl would render to
//      $tmp$HOME/.config/zellij/config.kdl and be deleted with the tmp
//      dir — it would never reach the desktop, and the failure is silent.
//   2. theme-doctor resolves every contract file as
//      `[[ -f "$STATE_DIR/$f" ]]`.
//   3. theme-parity resolves every contract file as
//      `"${RENDERED_DIRS[$target]}/$fname"`, i.e. `$tmp$STATE_DIR/$fname`.
// So output_path is ~/.local/state/theme/zellij.kdl (D-02), and commit.sh
// wires ~/.config/zellij/config.kdl to it with `ln -sf`, mirroring the
// yazi/satty/gtk-3.0/gtk-4.0 idiom already used four times in this
// repo. Measured THIS session that this shape live-reloads too: with
// ~/.config/zellij/config.kdl a SYMLINK to the state-dir file, a running
// session picked up an `rsync -a --delete` replacement of the symlink's
// target inode (commit.sh's own promotion mechanism) with the new fg SGR
// present and the old one entirely gone (8617 bytes captured).
//
// ── The themes block MUST stay MULTI-LINE, one colour per line (D-07) ──
// Measured THIS session: the collapsed single-line themes form is a KDL
// PARSE ERROR — zellij prints "Missing `;` after a node name..." and
// renders no session at all (a 1116-byte capture is what that failure
// looks like; a working session captures ~25680 bytes). Never collapse
// the themes block below onto one line.
//
// ── No reload hook exists or is needed (D-05) ──
// zellij watches its own config file and live-reloads a running session by
// itself through the symlink-plus-rsync mechanism measured above — the
// byte-count evidence at the top of this header (old fg SGR gone, new one
// present, no restart) is what proves it. This is a MEASURED decision,
// not an oversight: zellij needs no hook in lib/reload.sh at all. See
// lib/reload.sh's own zellij paragraph, beside the fan-out itself, for
// the same evidence recorded next to where a hook would otherwise sit.
//
// ── Role-assignment rule (follow without exception) ──────────────────
// A bare container role is a BACKGROUND and must never land in a colour
// slot on its own — the same category error fish-colors.fish and the
// fastfetch template both document.
// Every role chosen below is either a surface/on-surface pair or an
// `on_*` foreground role already trusted at measured-safe contrast by
// kitty-colors.conf (color5/color6's `on_tertiary_container`/
// `on_secondary_container`).
//
// ── Doubled-brace guard ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Two opening braces must never appear adjacent anywhere in the rendered
// output — theme-parity scans every contract file raw for a doubled-brace
// template leftover and would fail the file. Normal KDL formatting never
// does this; it is a rule for whoever edits this template next.
//
// Every colour value below is a matugen keyword (colors.<role>.default.hex)
// and no colour literal is hardcoded anywhere in this file.

theme "rice"

// ── Options ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Only what we mean; zellij's defaults are otherwise good.

// Matches kitty.conf. KDL has no conditional, so this cannot be guarded
// on the binary's presence the way a shell script could — but it is safe
// regardless, because install.sh declares fish in PACMAN_PKGS, so a
// reproduced machine always has it.
default_shell "fish"

// The wl-clipboard binary already declared in install.sh's PACMAN_PKGS
// gives zellij a native system-clipboard copy path. Without it zellij
// falls back to OSC 52.
copy_command "wl-copy"

// Session and pane-viewport state persist across a restart as BUILT-IN
// options — no plugin manager, no git clone and no headless fetch step
// needed for this surface at all.
session_serialization true
serialize_pane_viewport true

// So a fresh session is not hijacked by a release-notes pane.
show_release_notes false

// SET as of quick task 260820-1kp, superseding D-08's "deliberately
// unset". D-08's reasoning was correct for its own scope: leaving this
// unset is what made zellij's BUILT-IN powerline status bar render, and
// naming the compact bar instead would have discarded the wedge look.
// That trade no longer applies, because `rice` is not one of zellij's
// stock layouts — it is this repo's own, rendered from
// templates/zellij-layout.kdl and symlinked to
// ~/.config/zellij/layouts/rice.kdl by lib/commit.sh. It replaces the
// built-in bar with zjstatus, which draws the same wedge shape.
//
// Corrected 2026-08-20: an earlier version of this comment claimed the
// bar follows "all 20 palettes instead of the terminal's 8 ANSI slots".
// That is now exactly backwards. zjstatus was moved to NAMED colours
// precisely so it resolves through the 8-slot themes block below at draw
// time — which is what lets it re-theme LIVE. The hex version it replaced
// had the full role set and could not re-theme without a new session.
// See zellij-layout.kdl's header for the measurement behind that trade.
default_layout "rice"

// ── Background plugins ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// zellij-autolock switches to locked mode while a trigger command owns
// the pane, so a program with its own modal keymap (vim, fzf, an AI
// agent TUI) stops losing keystrokes to zellij's own bindings.
//
// It is loaded HERE rather than in the layout on purpose: a plugin in a
// layout needs a `pane`, and a pane costs a terminal row. autolock draws
// nothing, so paying a row for it would be a visible regression against
// the bar this task just added. `load_plugins` is zellij's mechanism for
// exactly this — a plugin loaded at startup with no surface of its own.
load_plugins {
    "file:~/.config/zellij/plugins/zellij-autolock.wasm" {
        is_enabled true
        triggers "nvim|vim|hx|helix|git|fzf|yazi|claude|less|man"
        watch_triggers "nvim|vim|hx|helix"
        watch_interval "1.0"
        reaction_seconds "0.3"
    }
}

// ── Keybinds ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Still almost none, and for the reason the original comment gave:
// zellij's defaults merge in unless explicitly cleared, and they are
// discoverable from the keybind-hint bar that zellij-layout.kdl puts
// back at the bottom. The two binds below are additive — they clear
// nothing and shadow nothing.
//
// Key choice is measured against zellij 0.44.3's own default mode keys
// (Ctrl g/p/t/n/h/s/o/q). Ctrl y and Ctrl f are both unclaimed there.
//
// BOTH TARGETS ARE ZELLIJ'S OWN IN-TREE PLUGINS, and that is a decision
// made on evidence rather than preference. This task originally bound
// these to two third-party .wasm plugins, room and monocle. monocle
// panicked on the operator's machine at src/main.rs:16 — 223 times in
// two minutes, a render loop — and it was released 2025-01-03, seventeen
// months before this zellij. The panic could not be reproduced across
// four separate probes, and a third-party Rust panic cannot be patched
// from here anyway. room did not fail, but carried the same rot risk
// from the same cause: an out-of-tree plugin pinned against a moving
// plugin API.
//
// `filepicker` and `session-manager` ship inside the zellij binary, so
// they are version-matched by construction and cannot drift out of
// compatibility the way monocle did. Prefer an in-tree plugin over a
// third-party one unless it genuinely cannot do the job.
//
// `shared_except "locked"` keeps these compatible with the autolock
// plugin above: while a trigger program holds the pane, the session is
// in locked mode and these binds correctly go silent rather than
// stealing Ctrl-f from the program that wanted it.
keybinds {
    shared_except "locked" {
        // session / tab switcher
        bind "Ctrl y" {
            LaunchOrFocusPlugin "session-manager" {
                floating true
            }
        }
        // file finder
        bind "Ctrl f" {
            LaunchOrFocusPlugin "filepicker" {
                floating true
            }
        }
    }
}

// ── Theme block (D-07: MULTI-LINE, one colour per line) ────────────────
// Eight named slots mirror kitty-colors.conf's already-measured ANSI
// mapping so the multiplexer chrome and the terminal palette cannot
// disagree; `orange` is a zellij-only slot with no kitty analogue,
// assigned an `on_*` foreground role of the same family kitty already
// trusts in color5/color6.
themes {
    rice {
        fg "{{colors.on_surface.default.hex}}"
        bg "{{colors.surface.default.hex}}"
        black "{{colors.surface_variant.default.hex}}"
        red "{{colors.error.default.hex}}"
        green "{{colors.tertiary.default.hex}}"
        yellow "{{colors.secondary.default.hex}}"
        blue "{{colors.primary.default.hex}}"
        magenta "{{colors.on_tertiary_container.default.hex}}"
        cyan "{{colors.on_secondary_container.default.hex}}"
        white "{{colors.on_surface_variant.default.hex}}"
        orange "{{colors.on_primary_container.default.hex}}"
    }
}
